\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Predicted survival probability from Cox proportional hazards models with linear (blue) and quadratic (orange) terms. The quadratic model shows a slight upward trend but the quadratic term is not significant ($p = 0.71$). Both models predict higher survival at higher knowledge redundancy, but the relationship is not statistically significant. Shaded areas represent 95\% confidence intervals.}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig2}{{2}{10}{Predicted survival probability from Cox proportional hazards models with linear (blue) and quadratic (orange) terms. The quadratic model shows a slight upward trend but the quadratic term is not significant ($p = 0.71$). Both models predict higher survival at higher knowledge redundancy, but the relationship is not statistically significant. Shaded areas represent 95\% confidence intervals}{figure.2}{}}
